  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "OMDSH Hub",
      "text": "OMDSH Hub is a community extension catalog and Profile generation manager for DeepSeek Harness. It reuses the Harness Profile, Bundle, Repository Plugin, Agent Preset, layered Skill registry, Cordis lifecycle, and configuration contracts while adding transactional installation, recovery, catalog browsing, and a settings UI."
    },
    {
      "section": "OMDSH Hub",
      "text": "This release candidate is checked against the newest packages currently published on the npm\n`next` channel (queried 2026-08-13): Cordis `4.0.1-rc.4` and the DSH client and Host contracts\n`0.0.1-rc.5`:\n\n- Bundle metadata under `package.json#dsh.bundle`;\n- Client metadata under `package.json#dsh.client`;\n- the `settings.section` client slot;\n- the `webServer` host service;\n- Loader readiness after every enabled Cordis fiber becomes active."
    },
    {
      "section": "OMDSH Hub",
      "text": "The package intentionally remains marked `private: true` to prevent npm publication. Making the GitHub repository public does not require removing that guard."
    },
    {
      "section": "Local validation",
      "text": "Use Node.js 22 or later:\n\n```bash\nnpm ci --ignore-scripts\nnpm run validate\nnpm run pack:check\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Local validation",
      "text": "The `@deepseek-ai` packages require registry read access. Supply a short-lived `NPM_TOKEN` through\nthe process environment and the local npm configuration described by the package owner; never put\na concrete token in this repository. `validate` checks the exact npm package versions and contract\ndeclarations, JavaScript syntax, the vendored Registry, and the complete Node test suite.\n`pack:check` inspects the package manifest without publishing it and rejects local npm configuration."
    },
    {
      "section": "Harness integration",
      "text": "The host entry is `dist/index.mjs`. It provides the extension manager, Workshop bridge, and agent ecosystem services, registers the loopback-only management API, and installs the `official-v2` runtime-ready adapter. `official-v2` is OMDSH's adapter API version; it is not a snapshot name."
    },
    {
      "section": "Harness integration",
      "text": "The prebuilt client entry is `dist/client.js`. It contributes the Extensions settings section through the standard client manifest and supports Installed, Discover, collections, recipes, updates, and history views."
    },
    {
      "section": "Harness integration",
      "text": "The npm registry did not provide `@deepseek-ai/dsh-repository-plugin` when this candidate was\nchecked. Git-source catalog entries therefore remain visible as guided integrations and OMDSH does\nnot claim that they can be installed through an npm-provided Repository Plugin. This repository\ndoes not copy a private or Git-snapshot implementation to fill that gap."
    },
    {
      "section": "Harness integration",
      "text": "The management endpoint is `/omdsh/extensions/v1`. Mutation requests are restricted to a loopback Host, reject cross-site Fetch Metadata, and require a matching HTTP Origin when an Origin header is present."
    },
    {
      "section": "Safety model",
      "text": "- Install and update operations are staged in a new physical Profile generation.\n- Package-manager lifecycle scripts are disabled by default.\n- Registry documents are strictly parsed and remote replacements require a configured Ed25519 signature.\n- A candidate generation becomes current only after configuration validation and runtime readiness confirmation.\n- Failed candidates are discarded and the previous generation remains recoverable."
    },
    {
      "section": "Documentation",
      "text": "- [Architecture](docs/architecture.md)\n- [Adapters](docs/adapters.md)\n- [Chinese README](README.zh.md)"
    },
    {
      "section": "License",
      "text": "MIT"
    }
